"},{"area":"legal","status":"flag","note":"Confirm Maryland disclosure requirements for automated AI (F4) with your attorney."},{"area":"operational","status":"block","note":"Confirm your version of Dentrix has the necessary API hooks for automated scheduling (F3)."},{"area":"financial","status":"pass","note":"The $150-$500/month cost is within range, but check for hidden middleware fees (F2, F3)."}]},"ai_tools_expert_r2":{"changed_position":false,"changed_because":"","rebuttals":[{"target":"devils_advocate","their_claim":"Replacing a human with AI creates unacceptable liability and operational risk.","response":"I agree the risk exists, but ignoring the 30% of lost leads (F5) is also a business failure. We can mitigate liability by keeping the AI focused strictly on scheduling, not clinical advice."},{"target":"strategist","their_claim":"If the AI doesn't integrate directly with Dentrix, it creates more work.","response":"You are right. My recommendation remains conditional on direct integration; if middleware is required, the complexity likely outweighs the efficiency gains for a one-person front desk."}],"concessions":["I agree with the Devil's Advocate that the AI should not handle clinical triage, only routine scheduling, to minimize liability (F7)."],"stance":"conditional","headline":"Proceed only if the vendor signs a BAA and integrates with Dentrix.","summary":"You can capture the 30% of calls you currently miss (F5), but only if the technology is secure and truly automated. Do not sign any contract unless the vendor provides a HIPAA-compliant BAA (F1) and performs a live, bidirectional sync with your specific version of Dentrix.","key_points":["AI can recover lost after-hours leads (F5), but you are legally responsible for any scheduling errors it makes (F7).","Demand a signed BAA from the vendor to remain HIPAA compliant (F1); have your attorney review this document.","Verify that your specific version of Dentrix allows direct API hooks for booking (F3); avoid third-party middleware if possible to ensure stability."],"risks":["HIPAA violations if the vendor fails to provide or maintain a valid BAA (F1).","Liability for scheduling errors caused by AI misinterpreting patient needs (F7).","Operational friction if the AI requires manual data entry instead of syncing to Dentrix (F3)."],"confidence":85,"pushback":"Are you certain your current internet connection is stable enough for voice processing, or will latency create a frustrating experience for your patients?","tools":[{"name":"NexHealth","use":"Automates appointment scheduling and syncs directly with Dentrix.","monthly_cost":"$300-500/mo","works_with":"Dentrix","caveat":"Must confirm compatibility with your specific Dentrix version."}]},"devils_advocate_r2":{"changed_position":false,"changed_because":"","rebuttals":[{"target":"industry_expert","their_claim":"Automated capture of after-hours leads could boost patient volume by 30%.","response":"Volume is irrelevant if the AI misbooks, offends a patient, or leaks data. A 30% increase in leads means nothing if the system creates a 100% increase in legal and reputational headaches."},{"target":"ai_tools_expert","their_claim":"AI can recover lost after-hours inquiries to increase patient intake.","response":"You are ignoring the 'garbage in, garbage out' risk. If the AI doesn't perfectly sync with your version of Dentrix, your front-desk staff will spend their entire morning fixing AI-generated booking errors (F3)."},{"target":"strategist","their_claim":"Capturing 30% of missed calls is smart for the business.","response":"It is not smart to offload high-trust triage to software that cannot distinguish between a routine cleaning and a dental emergency. You are trading professional judgement for a high-risk, unproven algorithm."}],"concessions":["I acknowledge that current after-hours processes are inefficient (F5)."],"stance":"oppose","headline":"Do not automate your front desk until you address high-stakes liability risks.","summary":"Automating your front desk is a gamble on unverified technology. You are legally liable for the AI's mistakes (F7). If the integration with Dentrix fails or the vendor lacks a HIPAA-compliant BAA, you face severe legal and operational consequences (F1, F3). Do not trade your staff's judgment for a risky, unproven software solution.","key_points":["You remain fully liable for any misinformation or scheduling errors the AI provides (F7).","Direct Dentrix integration is often non-existent, frequently requiring unreliable third-party middleware (F3).","Without a signed BAA, you risk direct violation of HIPAA privacy regulations (F1)."],"risks":["AI providing incorrect clinical instructions during triage.","Data privacy lawsuits from non-compliant AI handling sensitive patient information.","Increased administrative burden caused by fixing AI-driven scheduling errors."],"confidence":90,"pushback":"Question your assumption that an AI can manage your schedule as reliably as your trained staff without costing more in cleanup than you save in time."},"industry_expert_r2":{"changed_position":false,"changed_because":"","rebuttals":[{"target":"devils_advocate","their_claim":"The AI is too risky to replace human triage and oversight.","response":"Agreed, but our goal is capturing lost leads, not replacing triage. AI handles the simple scheduling; the front desk keeps the high-touch clinical decisions. We balance automation with human oversight."},{"target":"strategist","their_claim":"Integration issues might make the AI create more work for staff.","response":"Precisely why I am conditional. If it doesn't sync directly with Dentrix to write appointments, the overhead cost of cleaning up double-bookings will kill any ROI we expect."}],"concessions":["I accept that liability for AI scheduling errors sits entirely with the owner (F7)."],"stance":"conditional","headline":"Proceed only if the AI integrates directly with your Dentrix software.","summary":"Missing 30% of calls is losing money (F5). Automation helps, but only if it works perfectly with your data. Ensure the vendor signs a BAA (F1) and confirm your specific Dentrix version works with their API (F3). If it doesn't write directly to your calendar, skip it.","key_points":["Capturing after-hours leads could boost your patient base by up to 30% (F5).","Costs are likely within your $400 budget, but functionality varies widely (F2).","You can potentially leverage your existing RingCentral setup to avoid a total system migration (F6)."],"risks":["Technical glitches or incorrect scheduling for which you remain liable (F7).","Privacy violations if the AI vendor fails to provide a BAA (F1, verify with attorney).","Compliance fines for failing to disclose the use of AI to patients (F4, verify with licensing agency)."],"confidence":85,"pushback":"Is your internet connection stable enough to support real-time AI processing without latency that drops or frustrates patients?"}},"nodeInfo":{"path":"corkboard@1/round2@1","outputFor":["corkboard@1/round2@1"]},"id":"31e7685b-cc88-475f-a5b7-211f1d9c5fc6","timestamp":1793995931.8633337}

